# IT 140 Module Four Assignment
# Higher/Lower Game Pseudocode Template
#
# Complete the TODO prompts below with your own pseudocode.
# Keep this file in .pseudo format for submission.
#
# Use clear indentation to show decisions and repeated behavior.
# Your finished pseudocode should address every requirement in the
# current Module Four Assignment Guidelines and Rubric.

# Establish a valid guessing range.
# Ask the user for the lower and upper bounds.
OUTPUT "Enter the lower bound:"
INPUT lowerBound

OUTPUT "Enter the upper bound:"
INPUT upperBound

# Make sure the lower bound is less than the upper bound.
WHILE lowerBound >= upperBound
    OUTPUT "Invalid input. The lower bound must be less than the upper bound."

    OUTPUT "Enter the lower bound:"
    INPUT lowerBound

    OUTPUT "Enter the upper bound:"
    INPUT upperBound
END WHILE

# Establish the number the player is trying to guess.
# Generate a random number between the lower and upper bounds.
SET randomNumber = RANDOM NUMBER BETWEEN lowerBound AND upperBound

# Play the game.
# Ask the user for a guessing number and make sure it is within the bounds.
OUTPUT "Guess a number between " + lowerBound + " and " + upperBound + ":"
INPUT guess

WHILE guess < lowerBound OR guess > upperBound
    OUTPUT "Invalid guess. Please enter a number between " + lowerBound + " and " + upperBound + "."
    INPUT guess
END WHILE

# Continue playing the game until the user guesses the correct number.
WHILE guess != randomNumber

    # Compare the guess to the random number and give feedback to the user.
    IF guess < randomNumber
        OUTPUT "Your guess is too low."
    ELSE
        OUTPUT "Your guess is too high."
    END IF

    # Ask for another guess from the user when the game continues.
    OUTPUT "Guess again:"
    INPUT guess

    # Make sure the new guess is within the bounds.
    WHILE guess < lowerBound OR guess > upperBound
        OUTPUT "Invalid guess. Please enter a number between " + lowerBound + " and " + upperBound + "."
        INPUT guess
    END WHILE

END WHILE

# Alert the user when they guessed the correct number.
OUTPUT "Congratulations! You guessed the correct number."
